<<BD_INVOKE>> 2026-09-25T02:04:06.569905420+00:00 "comments" "add" "sim-o3kct" "--body" "Detector soundness, measured on feat/scxsim-cratesio-release-candidate: as mutation M4 (of four used to test symbol_export.rs), the sim_deterministic_mem.c definitions were given hidden visibility. known_gap_libc_takes_the_so_memory_functions then went red, as it should: the known-gap test fires when the fix sketched above is applied, so its red is trustworthy. The mutation was reverted; the arena-headroom and cross-allocator checks in the fix sketch were NOT done and still gate a real fix."
<<BD_INVOKE>> 2026-09-25T02:04:06.572686558+00:00 "comments" "add" "sim-0qzq6" "--body" "Interim state on feat/scxsim-cratesio-release-candidate: csrc/sim_wrapper.h now pins SCX_ENQ_IMMED to 0ULL explicitly (#undef + #define, marked DANGER TODO(sim-0qzq6)) instead of leaving it to the weak const volatile __SCX_ENQ_IMMED. Behaviour is unchanged (both read 0, i.e. a kernel without IMMED), but the weak global was reached through a relocation that the -rdynamic host's same-named copy interposes, which tests/symbol_export.rs (every_silent_binding_to_this_binary_is_listed) refuses. The fix this issue asks for is unchanged: undef it AND model the bounce-back through ops.enqueue (SCX_ENQ_REENQ); removing the pin alone would re-open the interposition."
