<<BD_INVOKE>> 2026-09-25T03:49:03.190537439+00:00 "comments" "add" "sim-4e4c0a" "--body" "Re-read at integration 24d864c6 (scx pin 413031d4) while preparing the crates.io release candidate. This is from reading the code. The nested-ancestor case was not re-run.

1. Upstream cgroup_bw no longer finds a cgroup's parent through the path described above. After the pin bump, lib/cgroup_bw.bpf.c computes the parent in `cbw_eff_parent_cgid()`. That walks `cbw_cgroup_ancestor()`, a CO-RE read of `cgrp->ancestors[level]`, and does not call the `bpf_cgroup_ancestor` kfunc. The field is now `eff_parent_id`, set in `cbw_init_cgx()`. The simulator's `sim_cgroup_alloc()` (csrc/sim_task.c) fills `ancestors[]` from the parent's array. So the NULL return this issue blames is no longer on the parent walk. cgroup_bw still calls `bpf_cgroup_ancestor(cgrp, 0)` to resolve the root.

2. The kfunc has three definitions today:
   - kfuncs.rs, in the host: looks the ancestor up in the cgroup registry (`sim_cgroup_lookup_ancestor`).
   - csrc/sim_bpf_stubs.c, in every .so: a weak fallback that returns NULL. It binds only when the host does not export the symbol. It is one of the 24 own_definition names in sim-3geoh.
   - schedulers/lavd/wrapper.c: a strong copy that returns the root for level 0 and NULL for every other level (a flat-hierarchy model). lavd uses it whatever the host exports.

3. Whether a nested cgroup without its own cpu.max is now bounded by its ancestor's limit needs a re-run. The #[ignore]d spec named above left with cgroup_bw_throttle_cycle.rs (929abf8). tests/cgroup_bw_throttle_unthrottle.rs `test_throttle_unthrottle_in_nested_hierarchy` limits the inner cgroup directly, so no test in the tree covers the ancestor case. If a re-run shows the ancestor limit now holds, this can close with a test. If not, the cause is somewhere other than the kfunc stub."
<<BD_INVOKE>> 2026-09-25T03:49:03.196526661+00:00 "comments" "add" "sim-c8949e" "--body" "Status check at integration 24d864c6, from the crates.io release candidate (tg scxsim-cratesio-release-candidate).

The release candidate recommends publishing scx_simulator as 0.1.0, not 1.0.0 (sim-rzyx9, item 2). One reason is that this tracker is still open. The other is that several fixes found by the release candidate change the public API.

The tracker is stale:
- It has 22 unchecked items. 18 name an issue, and 9 of those are closed: sim-09a30, sim-d80a1, sim-d46dd, sim-e5076, sim-ed0d6, sim-c3fd09, sim-ac6b5a, sim-466a13, sim-094402. Still open: sim-010a1, sim-880544, sim-80ce04, sim-943dc0, sim-d9988, sim-6b003, sim-c5dbf, sim-4c1e5, sim-d848e.
- Two unnamed items look done. 'SimCgroupHandle refactor': `CgroupInfo` (src/safe/cgroup.rs) now holds a `CgroupAlloc` whose variants wrap a `SimCgroupHandle`. 'cgroup.rs: move to safe/': the file is src/safe/cgroup.rs.
- The P3 item 'RAII migration for CgroupInfo (eliminate remaining unsafe Send/Sync)' has moved rather than gone. `CgroupInfo` has no unsafe impl now, but `CgroupPtr` and `SimCgroupHandle` carry `unsafe impl Send` and `unsafe impl Sync` in unsafe_impl/cgroup_wrapper.rs.
- The header names branch simulator.v4 at 15a3d0c. The development tip is now integration.

The release candidate filed 17 new issues under the label cratesio. sim-rzyx9 lists the ones it recommends fixing before any publish: sim-4xdj4, sim-0qpv9, sim-3geoh, sim-kuhrw, sim-6vhbq, sim-4b77c and sim-ld1ro (unsound or silently wrong for an in-process consumer); sim-cp5c0, sim-yrtox, sim-dneoq, sim-jnh26 and sim-fmijm (breaking to change after publication); and sim-kqri1 (licensing)."
<<BD_INVOKE>> 2026-09-25T03:49:03.204000584+00:00 "comments" "add" "sim-cxpef" "--body" "From the crates.io release candidate: scxtest/ has to be in scope, at least for scx_simulator's published files. sim-kqri1 has the detail.

- scxtest/ holds 9 files derived from upstream scx lib/scxtest, which upstream deleted at 54e1ea429. Two are identical to upstream's last version, and seven have been extended here.
- They are compiled into the published crates. scx_simulator's build.rs compiles scx_test.c, scx_test_map.c and scx_test_cpumask.c, and scxsim-build compiles overrides.c into every scheduler .so.
- None of the 9 has an SPDX line, a copyright notice or an origin note. They sit outside vendor/, so the only licence text next to them is the crate's BSD-3-Clause LICENSE, while the code is GPL-2.0.

The same packaged-file count applies to the header sweep here. Of scx_simulator's 272 packaged .c/.h/.rs files, 161 have no SPDX line."
